From google/pkcs11test (https://github.com/google/pkcs11test), Apache-2.0,
at the revision pinned in run.sh, applied after aes-fixture.patch. The token
generates no RSA keys, so pkcs11test's KeyPair fixture unwraps the RSA-2048
key run.sh wrapped for the token's unwrapping key (TSRA_PKCS11TEST_RSA_BLOB,
from rsa_blob.c) with CKM_RSA_AES_KEY_WRAP, and takes the public key the
unwrap leaves, found by a CKA_ID of the pair's own, instead of generating an
RSA-1024 pair. The headers pkcs11test vendors predate CKM_RSA_AES_KEY_WRAP,
hence its value and parameter layout inline. The context lines below are
upstream's. See README.md.

diff --git a/pkcs11test.h b/pkcs11test.h
--- a/pkcs11test.h
+++ b/pkcs11test.h
@@ -30,6 +30,8 @@
 #include <memory>
 #include <vector>
 #include <cstdlib>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <string>
 
 namespace pkcs11 {
 
@@ -275,22 +277,52 @@
